A||||7||LemonSky||How did Fieros do in govt crash tests?||||5||
Z||000000||LemonSky||08-14-2000||08:52 PM||||The questions says it all. I'm just curious because, while I love my Fiero, I've been apprehensive about its crash safety.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||86SE||08-14-2000||09:10 PM||||As far as I have heard Fieros got 5 star front rear and side impact rating.  They scored second highest in 84-88 right behind Volvo.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Stering wheel<BR>Gas AND brake petals<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||14
Z||000002||1FST2M6||08-14-2000||09:19 PM||||not right behind.. Right NEXT too volvo.. the NHTSA tested our toys and they are safe to play with...! (National Highway Traffic Safety Administration)||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||08-14-2000||09:22 PM||||Well I was colse  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I just looked at my NHTSA document (79-88 all vehicles tested) and it looks like the Fiero actually did beter than Volvo.<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Stering wheel<BR>Gas AND brake petals<BR>**Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention**||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||08-14-2000||09:31 PM||||Here are a few links to some interesting reading on Fiero safety. I hope this helps assure you that your Fiero is a safe car.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#FIERO" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#FIERO</A>  SAFETY<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mmit.com/ml320/crash.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mmit.com/ml320/crash.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/consumer.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/consumer.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/art-wreck.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000005||contra||08-14-2000||10:29 PM||||i would have to agree the fiero has 5 star front impact safety. i remember this winter in my '85 GT some honda riced up accord cut in front of me on slippery roads, and i couldn't stop in time, so i tboned the accord, and my car actually tore into the rear passenger door, and their back tire was in the back seat!. My car on the other hand just had a cracked bumper, fender, and headlight...and minimal frame bends.<BR>got it all fixed for under a grand canadian.<BR>the accord on the other hand was a write off...i got away with it all because they had no insurance.  kinda pissed me off a little tho because i just converted my 85 SE to the GT style, ground effects, fascias, sail panels, etc etc etc. took me 2 weeks! and then 5 days later those goofs damaged my car. ah well...i am now driving an 87 GT and i am selling the 85. But i hafta say, my 85 withstood the crash nicely, and i didn't get hurt at all. the accod crumpled like tinfoil!||||reg||1
Z||000006||wxxo||08-14-2000||10:49 PM||||for what its worth i give them 6 stars. ( i also found out the hard way how safe they are...im still typing arent i? haha)||||reg||1
